UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Three of Wands represents the absolute archetype of "Active Manifestation" and the strategic deployment of energy across the threshold of the known. Having successfully surveyed the horizon in the Two, the Three signifies the phase where the sovereign consciousness commits to the outbound journey, casting its intentions into the stream of time and space. This is the moment of the "long-range launch," where you have done the necessary preparation, established your baseline security, and are now observing the initial results of your deliberate projections as they return to you as opportunities or external signals. Visually depicted as a figure looking out toward the sea, watching the distant ships that carry the cargo of their creative endeavors, this archetype embodies the concept of "patient expectation"—the understanding that once the work is launched, it enters a self-sustaining feedback loop where your energy begins to interact with the broader, collective environment. Within the complex architecture of your consciousness, this is the stage of "kinetic resonance," where the gap between your internal drive and the external outcome begins to close. When the Three of Wands appears, your system is registering a "high-performance transit" status; you are no longer in the planning phase, but are actively witnessing the expansion of your influence into arenas you have only previously imagined. This card commands you to remain the observer—to maintain the perspective of the sovereign commander who knows that while the outcome is no longer under their direct, minute-to-minute control, it remains under the influence of their initial, high-frequency intent. You are being tasked with the essential work of "navigational alertness": being ready to pivot, to capitalize on the returning signals, and to expand your operations as the world responds to your initiative. To inhabit the Three of Wands is to master the art of "deliberate growth," recognizing that by stepping out of the defensive posture of the castle and into the active engagement with the world, you have transformed yourself from a static node into a dynamic, reality-shaping force. It is the ultimate validation that your strategic planning was not in vain, and that the universe is now, quite literally, moving to accommodate the vision you have dared to cast out into the distance.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Three of Wands appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "systemic feedback failure," "delayed activation," or the catastrophic loss of structural support for your outgoing initiatives. The reversal suggests that you have launched your energy into the world, but the expected return—the synergy, the growth, the validation—has failed to materialize, leading to a state of profound, chronic frustration where your "ships" seem to be drifting aimlessly in the fog. You are essentially "chasing ghosts," running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that attempts to force a result from a process that has either stalled or is fundamentally misaligned with the current environmental conditions. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to project an image of "ongoing success" or "impending arrival," while internally, you are paralyzed by the fear that your original vision was flawed, or worse, that your effort was wasted on a target that never existed. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of denial"; you are obsessively monitoring a horizon that is empty, refusing to accept the reality that your current trajectory requires a major course correction or a complete, systemic reboot. The reversed Three of Wands exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of acknowledging that your "big bet" failed, and the corresponding fear that admitting this failure would equate to a total loss of your sovereign standing. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these monitoring scripts, perform a brutal audit of your original assumptions, and confront the reality of why you are so hesitant to recall your energy and re-strategize. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance hope, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and disciplined reclamation of your sovereign agency. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of returning to the drawing board—accepting that the "stagnation" you feel is not a failure of the world to provide, but a signal that your current transmission is not hitting the necessary resonance, and that until you are willing to break the cycle of futile expectation, you will continue to be starved by the very projects you have launched without the necessary, high-level structural oversight.'
WHERE id = 17;
